      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Admitting a mistake is a far more damaging admission than a well-managed strategic pivot. Instead of a \"change of heart,\" we frame it as a necessary, albeit difficult, vote taken under extreme pressure from a specific, undisclosed faction within the party. This vague opposition makes the vote appear to be a political sacrifice for a greater good, not a personal failing. We then immediately transition to discussing how they will fight for that funding *next* time, showing proactive leadership.",
